diff --git a/CHANGELOG.en.md b/CHANGELOG.en.md
index 2d776ef..99bf812 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.en.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.en.md
@@ -8,7 +8,7 @@ Notable changes in Telsiz releases are listed in this file. Version numbers foll
 
 - The Telsiz DJ player can be moved: when the DJ card is not visible, the player in the corner of the screen can be dragged by its bar and dropped in one of the four corners, the Move button goes through the corners in turn, and the chosen corner is stored on the device. The default corner is the first one that does not cover the buttons of the radio card, the message box or the Room info button in the conversation header (between 760 and 1279 pixels the top right comes first, below the band and the conversation header). In a bottom corner the player moves above the message box and the radio card as long as there is room, as long as there is room it does not come down onto the card's buttons in any corner, and it stays inside the viewport in a short window too. While a layer that covers the main view, such as Settings, is open, the player sits in the bottom corner of the chosen side, and every row of Settings can be reached by scrolling. Minimize leaves only the bar: an audio file keeps playing, and a YouTube track pauses on that device only and resumes in sync with the room with Show. The Floating Player switch keeps the player in the corner even while the card is visible, and an audio file then also shows in the corner with its waveform and bar. The name of the playing track and "Telsiz DJ · room" are given to your system's media controls and lock screen (Media Session), which can be turned off in the Media controls section of Settings > Privacy. Play and Pause there only affect that device and do not stop the room's music, and that pause is also lifted by the `/resume` command and when you leave the voice room. The bar of the player in the corner shows a pause on that device (and a minimized YouTube track) with an unlit lamp, and its Resume on This Device button resumes on that device only without pausing the room. When someone else adds a track to Telsiz DJ in your voice room, a line with the track's name appears in the Notifications list, and these lines do not push the line of an ongoing screen share with its Watch button out of the list.
 - Search by song name in Telsiz DJ: if the owner has turned it on, a command such as `/play lobby song` makes the server search YouTube for the song name and add the first playable result to the queue with its name, and the announcement goes out with the name right away. The search does not use the official YouTube API and goes against YouTube's Terms of Service, which is why it is off by default and the owner turns it on in Settings > General > Music bot through a confirmation dialog. The search text is not encrypted: it goes to the server and, from the server's IP address, to YouTube. The client's address does not go to YouTube, and the text is not logged. There are at most 10 searches per minute per person and 300 YouTube requests in the last 24 hours across the server, and results stay in a cache for 10 minutes. If YouTube changes its format or blocks the server's address, the search turns off for 1 hour after repeated failures and a warning is written to the log. While search is off or fails, a clear error message and a Search on YouTube link on the DJ card appear. Adding by link always works. The search has never been tried against the real YouTube, and the first live test has to be done on the server ([docs/DEPLOYMENT.md](docs/DEPLOYMENT.md#youtube-search-by-song-name)).
-- Automatic idle: if the mouse, keyboard, touch or a gamepad is not used on a device for 10 minutes, that device counts as idle, and once all of a person's open devices are idle, others see the person as Idle and the person's own status reads "Idle (automatic)". The first input brings them back to Online. A device in a voice room never counts as idle, the desktop app also counts use of other apps on the computer, and the background windows of frequencies that are not open decide by the system idle time. A chosen Idle, Do Not Disturb or Invisible status does not change. The information goes to the server's memory with the long-poll request (`idle`) and is not written to disk, and a session going idle is accepted at most once every 5 seconds. It can be turned off for this device in the Automatic Idle section of Settings > Privacy, where the time (5, 10, 15, 30 or 60 minutes) can be chosen. The server and members can see when a person went inactive.
+- Automatic idle: if the mouse, keyboard, touch or a gamepad is not used on a device for 10 minutes, that device counts as idle, and once all of a person's open devices and tabs are idle, others see the person as Idle and the person's own status reads "Idle (automatic)". The first input brings them back to Online. A device in a voice room never counts as idle, the desktop app also counts use of other apps on the computer, and the background windows of frequencies that are not open decide by the system idle time. A chosen Idle, Do Not Disturb or Invisible status does not change. The information goes to the server's memory with the long-poll request (`idle` and the page id `tab`) and is not written to disk, and a session going idle is accepted at most once every 5 seconds. Since the tabs of the same browser share one session, the report of each page is kept apart, so a tab in use and a forgotten tab do not take turns changing the status. It can be turned off for this device in the Automatic Idle section of Settings > Privacy, where the time (5, 10, 15, 30 or 60 minutes) can be chosen. The server and members can see when a person went inactive.
 
